  "verified": [
    "Actual SPIR-V -> NIR -> ACO compute shader produces 80 bytes of AMD code / 60 executable bytes; public pipeline, descriptor-set layout/pool/update, SSBO, push constant and dispatch use native resources.",
    "Actual vertex/fragment graphics pipeline, optimal 64x64 RGBA8 GFX9 image/view, device-local binding, render pass/framebuffer/clear/draw, image-to-buffer copy and transfer-to-host barrier record 544 PM4 dwords.",
    "Compute command buffer on family1 executes a secondary fill stream and a transfer-to-compute barrier; public binary semaphore links it to graphics family0. The fixture records both native engines and a real submitted dependency.",
    "Pipeline-cache reuse, public export/import/rebuild, plus truncated shader payloads and inconsistent debug-data sizes are exercised against actual RADV cache code.",
    "Public callback OOM, malformed SPIR-V returning VK_ERROR_UNKNOWN, native BO reserve/bind OOM and map failure leave pipeline handles NULL. A subsequent valid public pipeline compiles successfully.",
    "UINT32_MAX recording reservation and NULL emit array produce no memory access after discard, preserve the storage canary and return OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY from finalize. Reset permits a fresh valid stream.",
    "Public stale-completion WaitForFences and a subsequent QueueSubmit report DEVICE_LOST; prior winsys tests cover map retry, bounded submit failure, timeout, native resource retention and independent fault owner.",
    "Actual R4SYS compiler threads exit and are joined before CPU results or arena storage change ownership. Vulkan allocation callback counts balance after physical/logical device destruction."
  ],
